    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d811">

                <pb facs="0903" n="709" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg709"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Rumania)/7–2345:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 811<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Representative in Rumania</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Melbourne</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bucharest</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-23T19:00:00+02:00">July 23, 1945—7 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>495. See Telegram M–1285 July 23 [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">24</hi>]<anchor n="1" xml:id="d811-f1"/> sent by
                        Schuyler to War
                    Dept outlining and asking for comment on his
                    proposed course of action in view of Soviet proposed ACC procedure. General considers and I concur it is necessary to
                    make clear American viewpoint on significant continuing unilateral actions taken
                    by Soviet officials on ACC or risk assumption
                    that now they are countenanced by Schuyler.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Melbourne</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
